sray – Ray on Slurm helper
==========================

`sray` is a small Python script that starts a Ray head node on the current
machine and provisions Ray workers on a Slurm cluster using `srun`.

Usage
-----

```bash
python sray.py --nodes 4 --cpus-per-node 8 --gpus-per-node 1 --partition gpu
```

Options include:

* `--nodes`: total nodes to allocate (default: 2)
* `--gpus-per-node`: GPUs to request for each node (default: 0)
* `--cpus-per-node`: CPUs to request for each node (default: 4)
* `--mem-per-node`: Slurm-style memory string per node (default: 16G)
* `--partition`: optional Slurm partition
* `--dashboard-port`: dashboard port (default: 8265)
* `--port`: Ray head GCS port (default: 6379)
* `--ray-client-port`: Ray client port (default: 10001)

Stop the script with Ctrl+C to release the cluster resources.
